    "title": "Chris Paul's Return to the Clippers Ends Abruptly",
    "text": "• Chris Paul's return to the Los Angeles Clippers has ended.\n• The decision was made by Clippers basketball operations president Lawrence Frank.\n• Frank informed Paul of the decision in a meeting in Atlanta that ended around 2 a.m. Wednesday.\n• Frank stated the decision was made on Sunday.\n• Frank said the decision had multiple layers and was not due to one incident.\n• Paul announced the news on social media shortly before 3 a.m. Wednesday.\n• The Clippers were in Atlanta for a road game against the Hawks on Wednesday night.\n• The Clippers' flight to Atlanta from Miami on Tuesday was delayed for about 4 1/2 hours.\n• Paul is in his 21st NBA season and hinted at retirement last month.\n• Paul is a 12-time All-Star and two-time Olympic gold medalist.\n• Paul ranks second in NBA history with 12,552 assists.\n• Clippers coach Tyronn Lue stated the decision was not because of Paul.\n• Paul played for the Clippers from 2011-17, leading the team to six winning seasons.\n• Paul rejoined the Clippers as a free agent last July.\n• Frank stated the move was not due to underperformance and that Paul had nothing to do with it.\n• The Clippers will likely try to trade Paul.\n• A trade cannot happen until Dec. 15.\n• Paul is averaging 2.6 points and 3.3 assists in 14.3 minutes per game.\n• The Clippers are on a five-game losing streak.\n• The Clippers are tied with Sacramento for the second-worst record in the Western Conference.\n• Leonard has been limited to 10 games by injuries.\n• Bradley Beal is out for the season due to hip surgery.",
